=== Live connection test (Merchandising.Tests.Integration/ConnectionFactoryTests.vb) ===

Test opens a real connection via ConnectionFactory.CreateOpenConnectionAsync() using
DatabaseOptionsLoader.Load() (default path = the ACL-protected file above), then queries
@@SESSION.sql_mode and @@SESSION.tx_isolation on that same connection.

$ dotnet test src/tests/Merchandising.Tests.Integration/Merchandising.Tests.Integration.vbproj --filter "ConnectionFactoryTests" -v normal

  Passed OpenedConnection_HasStrictModeAndReadCommittedIsolation [394 ms]

Test Run Successful.
Total tests: 1
     Passed: 1

Assertions made inside the test:
  - connection.State = Open
  - @@SESSION.sql_mode contains "STRICT_TRANS_TABLES"
      (appended via `SET SESSION sql_mode = CONCAT(@@SESSION.sql_mode, ',STRICT_TRANS_TABLES')`
      on every connection the factory opens — belt-and-braces with the P1-04 my.ini change,
      so a XAMPP reinstall or a reverted my.ini cannot silently bring back the truncation
      behaviour demonstrated at P0-07/ADR-003.2)
  - @@SESSION.tx_isolation = "READ-COMMITTED" exactly
      (`SET SESSION tx_isolation = 'READ-COMMITTED'` — the 10.4 variable name; the MySQL 8 /
      MariaDB 11 name `transaction_isolation` does not exist here and raises ERROR 1193,
      confirmed not used anywhere in this code, per CLAUDE.md section 6.2)

